ge/jaoe38c1m03vr3lu/27c55477-48e6-4b41-a16c-b51747fb2b91/ee2eee20-5fbf-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vr3lv.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m03vr3lu/27c55477-48e6-4b41-a16c-b51747fb2b91/ee2eee20-5fbf-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vr3lv.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m03vr3lu/27c55477-48e6-4b41-a16c-b51747fb2b91/ee2eee20-5fbf-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vr3lv.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m03vr3lu/27c55477-48e6-4b41-a16c-b51747fb2b91/ee2eee20-5fbf-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vr3lv.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The product 2,3-dimethyl but-2-ene undergoes ozonolysis to form two moles acetone.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 37 English Explanation 4\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1m03vsmmc/54746e98-3b9a-4430-8e92-6382e28a66b9/18ae2440-5fc0-11ef-9c8f-2bd8696d9aab/file-jaoe38c1m03vsmmd.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Two moles of acetone is the final product of the reaction.</p>\n<p>Compound P is 3,3-dimethyl butyne.</p>"}]}